#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115433 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Trigonometric Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84b6222b-1e46-596b-b52a-dd5c29bc51aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112042} {:answer/id #uuid "9c625d6b-5cc1-5311-8196-bc5fb2b668ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2πn" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112043} {:answer/id #uuid "a5689e92-eb4f-576a-8945-e47dea3236b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2} + 2πn" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112044} {:answer/id #uuid "decc828b-46d3-5e6e-a93e-d45e144952cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "πn" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112045} {:answer/id #uuid "585ffa58-eda2-55a9-b382-6fb65de297f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{πn}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "585ffa58-eda2-55a9-b382-6fb65de297f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{πn}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112046} :answer-field/id #uuid "0afa0019-b756-5b1b-84f0-0b7722ce646a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1331c2bd-7afa-50b7-b047-4451e8684c1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-162528" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=t\\,i+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2t)\\,j+(1+{t}^{2})\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n2t=\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $1+{t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348175 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Trigonometric Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bc502d3-9a60-5405-a2ed-1dbed2532bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348177} {:answer/id #uuid "c2209042-3cbe-552c-92a8-70ade799ba0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348178} {:answer/id #uuid "95ca12fc-19a7-5548-9f63-63504ebb620b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348179} {:answer/id #uuid "8cfa790f-86ec-5569-bcd7-0d940484cf39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348180} {:answer/id #uuid "ba3c6d41-46fe-50bc-a32f-ce6218800926" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bc502d3-9a60-5405-a2ed-1dbed2532bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348177} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ef4e86f-865e-5090-ad52-6a1a01a7ae04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2987e81-f85b-5262-9ea2-835ea44d86e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162644" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(t+1)\\,i+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)\\,j+{e}^{-t}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348182 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Trigonometric Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9fcbf32-332c-5c87-8210-6deb57760444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348184} {:answer/id #uuid "423e8eba-036b-5e3d-be47-525926b9195a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348185} {:answer/id #uuid "24f6973c-0c88-5443-84d5-46c788c622d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348186} {:answer/id #uuid "7aaf2296-900e-57b2-809c-0bac2adc3072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi n}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348187} {:answer/id #uuid "11af6d97-de7f-508a-8770-6a8e2bb88db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24f6973c-0c88-5443-84d5-46c788c622d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348186} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca7b4f86-3644-5d4f-a072-20fc956b1eae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1976d30c-74aa-51d8-aaf6-6704e25dfbc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162645" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)={t}^{3}\\,i+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,j+\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component ${t}^{3}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\nt+\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348189 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a1499c-080d-5008-bcc3-492ef469d3dc" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Exponential and Logarithmic Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f96ba185-5cc1-55df-96ce-939432327fc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\in [0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348191} {:answer/id #uuid "c5164973-2211-5fcb-906d-885461c0560f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\in [0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348192} {:answer/id #uuid "34214326-db20-5c52-9641-33e6e7ab79dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\in (1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348193} {:answer/id #uuid "af70a985-d621-53c3-a444-f7e0107b5a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\in [0,2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348194} {:answer/id #uuid "42e83a92-c0b4-5fc4-919e-23052075a3a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\in (-\\infty ,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5164973-2211-5fcb-906d-885461c0560f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\in [0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348192} :answer-field/id #uuid "80a3e29d-befd-52a7-a0e1-3d4912ff373f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c49d334-bc59-54a3-bdf0-55aa80dbe3ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-162659" :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=⟨\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-s),\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\sqrt{s}$ is $s\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,2).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{3}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersecti